      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is Yan Qing, the same young East Asian man from Picture 1, with the same black hair, face, plain dark short-sleeve shirt and dark trousers. Keep his identity and proportions stable; from this rear three-quarter view his face is only partly visible, so do not turn him toward camera.\n<Subject 2> is the exact same dark blue-black step-through electric bicycle in Picture 1, with the same round rear lamp, frame, wheels, seat, mirrors and rear rack. It is already carrying one tan kraft-paper-wrapped pork parcel, strapped flat and secure behind the seat.\n<Subject 3> is the same single wrapped pork parcel. Keep it on the rear rack for the entire clip; it does not open, slide, multiply or fall.\n<Picture 1> is the approved generated opening keyframe for this exterior return-home shot. It fixes the opening rider pose, bike, parcel, road layout, trees, lamps, buildings, parked scooters, dawn exposure, camera angle and screen direction.\n\nsummary:\nOne uninterrupted wide rear three-quarter shot: Yan Qing rides the loaded e-bike calmly away from the camera along the quiet residential street, returning home after buying meat. The same parcel stays securely on the rear rack. The road and camera remain stable.\n\nretention_analysis:\nPreserve the exact road, vanishing point, curb lines, tree rows, residential fences/buildings, streetlights, parking shelter and parked scooters from Picture 1. Preserve the rider's clothes and the same bike and single parcel. He continues forward away from camera, getting gradually smaller in the frame. Do not turn, reverse, stop, dismount or change screen direction. Do not introduce anyone else or any moving traffic. Keep the same cool dawn and practical streetlamp lighting; do not make the scene brighter, sunnier, wetter or more dramatic than Picture 1.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic natural live-action drama, quiet early morning after the market errand. Static wide camera from slightly behind and to the left, matching Picture 1; no camera pan, tilt, zoom, shake or cut. Natural bicycle speed and human movement, understated rather than commercial.\n\nOne continuous 7.29-second action:\n0.0-1.0s The rider is already seated and begins rolling gently forward, both hands on the handlebars. The parcel remains strapped behind the seat.\n1.0-5.8s He rides steadily away along the center-left side of the empty street toward the existing vanishing point. The bicycle wheels rotate naturally; his body and clothing move subtly with the ride. The static street geometry does not shift.\n5.8-7.29s He continues in the same direction and recedes farther into the distance. End while still riding away, with the same single parcel visible on the rack.\n\nNo dialogue is required; audio is not being evaluated. No subtitles, captions, logos, readable signs or watermarks. No second rider, pedestrian, car or new scooter. No changed face, outfit, vehicle design, parcel or street layout. No advertising pose, product close-up, dramatic commercial lighting, artificial motion blur, cartoon, anime or flat 3D render.",
